      "extract": "Hopf solitons arise in theories in three-dimensional space where the field takes values in a two-sphere. The Skyrme-Faddeev model [@Fa2] is the most famous example of a theory with Hopf solitons and consists of the $O(3)$ sigma model modified by the addition of a Skyrme term that is quartic in the derivatives of the field. Substantial numerical work [@FN; @GH; @BS5; @HS; @Su] has led to a reasonable understanding of",
